## Context

In `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf` (Figure 4 of
`slides/manuscript/main.md`), the Coherence-group column labelled "Capacity≥0"
renders as **"Capacityz0"** — the `≥` glyph falls back in matplotlib's PDF
backend (the default font lacks U+2265). The PNG backend renders it correctly,
so it only shows in the committed PDF that the manuscript includes.

This is pre-existing (the label string `COLUMN_LABELS["coherence_capacity_nonnegative"]
= "Capacity≥0"` predates ticket 0487 and was left untouched there per scope) and
purely cosmetic, but it is review-visible in a manuscript figure on the path to
the reviewable arXiv PDF.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` — `COLUMN_LABELS` dict (the `"Capacity≥0"` entry) and the matplotlib setup in `make_figure()`
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf` — regenerated artifact

## Actions

1. Pick the lightest robust fix:
   - **Option A (recommended):** change the label to `"Capacity ≥0"` rendered via
     mathtext (`r"Capacity $\geq$0"`) so matplotlib typesets the relation with its
     math font (no system-font dependency).
   - **Option B:** ASCII fallback `"Capacity≥0"` → `"Capacity≥0"`/`"Cap. nonneg."`
     (avoids the glyph entirely; less precise).
   - Avoid font-substitution config (fragile across CI/local matplotlib installs).
2. Regenerate the PDF via the `render.mk` heatmap target.
3. Visually confirm the label reads "Capacity ≥0" (or chosen text) in the PDF.

## Test

Extend `tests/test_plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py`: assert the rendered
column label for `coherence_capacity_nonnegative` contains a `≥`/`\geq`
construct, OR (backend-agnostic) assert `COLUMN_LABELS["coherence_capacity_nonnegative"]`
uses the mathtext form. Prefer a source-level assertion over PDF byte inspection.

## Verification

- [ ] Heatmap PDF column label no longer reads "Capacityz0"
- [ ] PDF regenerated via the DAG target
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- Do not change the veto-column handling or any genuine sub-score coloring (0487 scope)
- Do not alter the data or the disqualification logic — label-only change

## Exit criteria

- Label renders correctly in the committed PDF; all verification boxes ticked
